problems.problem:
Find all natural numbers $N$ satisfying the following two conditions:
– only two of the digits of $N$ are different from $0$, and one of them is $3$;
– $N$ is a perfect square.

$10000$ points are marked on a circle and numbered from $1$ to $10000$ clockwise. $5000$ straight segments are drawn in such a way that the following three conditions hold:
– each segment joins two of the marked points;
– each marked point belongs to one and only one segment;
– each segment intersects exactly one of the other segments.
Each segment is associated with the product of the numbers assigned to its two endpoints. Let $S$ be the sum of the products associated with all the segments.
Prove that $S$ is a multiple of $4$.

A player places a token on a cell of an $m\times n$ board divided into $1\times 1$ cells. The player moves the token according to the following rules:
– in each move, the player moves the token from the cell where it is to one of the cells that share a side with it;
– the player may not place the token on a cell it has previously occupied;
– two consecutive moves may not have the same direction.
The game ends when the player cannot move the token. Determine all the values of $m$ and $n$ for which the player can place the token on some cell such that it has occupied all the cells at the end of the game.
